       'An insured carries a limit ABOVE the coinsurance requirement. A partial loss occurs. How does the extra insurance affect the payment?', 'Once the did/should fraction reaches 1 there is nothing left for coinsurance to reduce. **Insurance never pays more than the loss**, so over-insuring buys nothing but a larger premium.', 'draft'
