       'A policy has a $1,000,000 per-occurrence limit and a $2,000,000 aggregate. Claims of $800,000 and $700,000 have already been paid this period. A third claim of $900,000 arrives. What is paid?', 'The aggregate is the cap for the whole policy period. $800,000 + $700,000 = $1,500,000 paid, leaving **$500,000** of the $2,000,000 aggregate. The per-occurrence limit would have allowed the full $900,000, but the aggregate runs out first — and once it is exhausted the policy is finished for the period even though months may remain.', 'draft'
